-- #845 (drained by #1114): the SELECTIVE spelling of a cross-module callee whose
-- constraint is INFERRED.  `lib/obl1114_inferred.mdk`'s `f` is `Num a => a -> a`, so
-- `f "abc"` has no discharge; DICT-SEMANTICS §4.2 D1 makes it a check-time reject.
--
-- BEFORE #1114 this was the #845 pin, and it broke every arm of this gate at once:
-- `check` exited 0 with no diagnostic, `run` exited 1 by RUNNING the program into
-- `E-PANIC: unknown op '+'`, and `build` exited 0 writing a binary that SEGFAULTED
-- (exit 139).  The cross-module store the check path reads held only DECLARED contexts,
-- so an unsignatured export's inferred one was dropped at every importing call site.
import lib.obl1114_inferred.{f}

main = println (f "abc")
